.TH PUTIO-SYNC 1 "November 2025" "putio-sync 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
putio-sync \- CLI tool for syncing files from Put.io to local storage
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B putio-sync
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B putio-sync
is a command-line tool for downloading and managing files from Put.io cloud storage service.
It provides comprehensive features for file synchronization, download management, and automation.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
Path to configuration file (default: ~/.config/putio-sync/config.toml)
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Increase verbosity (can be used multiple times: -v, -vv, -vvv)
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress output except errors
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help information
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version information
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B login
Authenticate with Put.io using OAuth token
.TP
.B files list
List files and folders from Put.io
.TP
.B files delete
Delete files from Put.io
.TP
.B download
Download files from Put.io to local storage
.TP
.B transfers add
Add torrents to Put.io
.TP
.B transfers list
List active transfers
.TP
.B history
View download and delete history
.TP
.B stat
Display download statistics
.TP
.B server
Start HTTP API server in daemon, watch, or download modes
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Login with OAuth token:
.B putio-sync login
.TP
List all files:
.B putio-sync files list
.TP
Download all files to current directory:
.B putio-sync download
.TP
Start daemon mode for continuous syncing:
.B putio-sync server --daemon
.TP
Add torrent from magnet link:
.B putio-sync transfers add "magnet:?xt=..."
.TP
View download statistics:
.B putio-sync stat
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration is stored in TOML format at:
.B ~/.config/putio-sync/config.toml

Example configuration:
.nf
[auth]
oauth_token = "YOUR_TOKEN_HERE"
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/putio-sync/config.toml
User configuration file
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/putio-sync/downloads.db
SQLite database for download history
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Set logging level (error, warn, info, debug, trace)
.TP
.B PUTIO_SYNC_CONFIG
Override default configuration file path
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success
.TP
.B 1
General error
.TP
.B 2
Configuration error
